    "canonicalStory": "Tammy Duckworth served as a Black Hawk helicopter pilot in the Illinois Army National Guard. In November 2004, her helicopter was struck by a rocket-propelled grenade in Iraq. She lost both legs and partial use of her right arm. Her crewmates and medical teams helped keep her alive. Recovery at Walter Reed required surgeries, rehabilitation, prosthetics, and a redefinition of daily life. Duckworth has repeatedly emphasized that survival was not an individual triumph detached from others; it was made possible by her crew and by systems of military medicine and support. She later led the Illinois Department of Veterans' Affairs, served as an Assistant Secretary of Veterans Affairs, and entered Congress. Her life did not return to the exact course she had imagined. Service changed form---from flying missions to advocating for veterans, disability access, military families, and public policy.",
