    "canonicalStory": "Lauren Wasser was a young model when she developed toxic shock syndrome, a rare but life-threatening illness associated with bacterial toxins and, in some cases, tampon use. She experienced organ failure and severe complications. Her right leg was amputated below the knee; years of pain and damage eventually led to the amputation of her left leg as well. Recovery involved repeated medical treatment, prosthetics, pain, grief, and rebuilding a career. Wasser returned to modeling and athletics, but the deeper public role became advocacy: speaking about menstrual-product safety, warning signs, and the need for clearer education and research. Her story should not be reduced to \"beauty despite disability\" or a product scare. Toxic shock is rare, medically complex, and requires accurate health guidance. The inspiration is her decision to convert an isolating crisis into credible public attention for a risk many people barely understand.",
