    "canonicalStory": "In 1967, seventeen-year-old Joni Eareckson dove into shallow water and sustained a spinal cord injury that left her with quadriplegia. Months of hospitalization and rehabilitation were followed by depression and the difficult work of learning a life requiring extensive assistance. Tada learned to draw and paint holding tools with her mouth, wrote books, recorded music, and founded an organization serving people with disabilities. Her Christian faith is central to her own interpretation of the story and should be represented accurately without suggesting that disability exists to teach others a lesson. Across decades, Tada has also faced chronic pain, breast cancer, and respiratory illness. Her life resists the neat \"comeback\" ending. Adaptation is ongoing, support is necessary, and meaningful work can coexist with grief, dependence, and unresolved physical difficulty.",
