    "canonicalStory": "Foreman entered professional boxing with fearsome power and became heavyweight champion while still in his twenties. His identity was built around dominance. After losing to Muhammad Ali and later suffering another defeat, Foreman stepped away from boxing. Years passed. The sport moved on, and few imagined a serious return. Foreman came back older, heavier, calmer, and strategically different. He no longer relied only on intimidation. He used patience, experience, and a public personality that contrasted sharply with his younger self. In 1994, at age 45, Foreman knocked out Michael Moorer and regained the heavyweight championship, becoming the oldest heavyweight champion at that time. Sometimes the comeback is possible because you are no longer trying to be the person you were the first time.",
