    "canonicalStory": "Fraser became a major film star through adventure, comedy, and dramatic roles. His physical performances brought success but also placed heavy demands on his body. Injuries, surgeries, personal hardship, and professional disruption contributed to years in which he appeared far less prominently. Public understanding of that absence was incomplete. Fraser continued working, accepted roles that differed from his earlier image, and eventually delivered a deeply vulnerable performance in The Whale. The role earned him the Academy Award for Best Actor and produced one of Hollywood's most warmly received career returns. Being less visible does not mean your value has disappeared. A quieter season may be rebuilding capacities the public cannot see.",
