    "canonicalStory": "As a teenager, Seles became one of tennis's dominant champions, known for fierce concentration and relentless two-handed strokes. In 1993, a spectator attacked her on court in Hamburg. The physical wound healed sooner than the psychological trauma. Her career stopped at the height of her powers. Seles took the time she needed rather than performing recovery for public comfort. She eventually returned in 1995, carrying a challenge no training program could fully simulate. She won her first tournament back and later reached the Australian Open final, adding major achievements after the attack. Returning after trauma is not about proving the event did not affect you. It is about deciding what parts of your life you still want to reclaim.",
    "decision": "She chose to return when she was ready---not when the world demanded a comeback.",
