    "canonicalStory": "Johnson was one of basketball's brightest stars, leading the Los Angeles Lakers with joy, creativity, and championship success. His HIV diagnosis forced immediate retirement and placed him at the center of a public-health crisis surrounded by stigma and misunderstanding. Johnson chose visibility. He spoke publicly, sought treatment, and used his platform to educate people about HIV and challenge false assumptions about who could be affected. He returned briefly to basketball, built a major business career, and became one of the world's most recognizable long-term examples of living with HIV. A diagnosis can change the plan without eliminating purpose. Honest visibility can become service to people you may never meet.",
    "decision": "He chose to face the public and use fear as an opportunity for education.",
    "reelspiration": "A diagnosis can change your life without becoming the only definition of it.",
    "principle": "Hope becomes credible when it includes treatment, truth, and sustained action.",
