    "whyItMatters": "This connects with people facing a frightening diagnosis and with anyone afraid that public truth will erase how others see them.",
    "reelScriptAuthored": "In 1991, Magic Johnson stood before the world and announced that he was\nliving with HIV. At the time, the diagnosis carried enormous fear,\nmisinformation, and stigma. Johnson retired immediately from\nbasketball---but he refused to disappear. He sought treatment, spoke\npublicly, challenged false beliefs, and used his platform to educate\nmillions. He later returned briefly to the game, built a major business\ncareer, and continued living openly for decades. Today's Reelspiration:\na diagnosis can change your life without becoming the only definition of\nit. Hope is not denial. It is truth, treatment, support, and the\ndecision to keep building purpose inside a reality you did not choose.",
